{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-23T16:33:17.327Z","data":{"text":"Task 3 is complete. Both gates pass.\n\n**What I did**\n\n- Added `src/core/report/approval-flags.ts`: reads `approvalFlags` from each active/archived change's `.run/manifest.json`, skips folders without a valid recorded field (never recomputing), and counts per flag id plus `none` how many changes fired the flag and how many later had trouble (task-stream `dead`, or task/change-stream `regressed`), split by `shown`/`confirmed`. Key order is typed against `ApprovalFlagId` so it cannot silently drift from the digest.\n- Extended `MetricsReport` with `approvalFlags`, filled it in `getMetricsReport`, and rendered the `Approval flags:` text block between the planning and cycle sections via a helper (grandfathered functions stay wired, not grown).\n- Emitted the field through `toStableMetrics` and regenerated `fixture/report/expected.json` — the only diff is the zeroed `approvalFlags` block.\n- Updated `tests/report-json.test.ts` (key lists, hand-built reports, text/shape assertions) and added `tests/report-approval-flags.test.ts` covering shown/confirmed, dead/regressed and clean changes, `none`, a legacy manifest without the field, and invalid/malformed manifests, asserting `changes` and every count.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- Task verify (`node --import tsx --test tests/report-approval-flags.test.ts tests/report-json.test.ts`): 15 pass.\n- Proposal verify (`pnpm verify`): exit 0."}}
